  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Hot and humid weather likely next week.\n\nMid to upper level ridging will begin to build across the Great \nLakes this weekend, bringing a major pattern change to the area. \nThis ridge will amplify and intensify as it reaches the eastern \nCONUS throughout next week. As heights build to around 596 dm next \nweek across the Ohio Valley, a hot and humid air mass will push into \nwestern and north central New York, resulting in the potential for \nmultiple days of 90+ degree weather and even hotter heat indices \nfrom Tuesday through Friday. This being said, heat-related headlines \nwill be likely during this period, especially as the likelihood for \ndangerous heat indices increase. Some relief from the heat is \npossible during the mid week period with the potential for showers \nand thunderstorms, but predictability is too low at this forecast \nrange.",
